  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract obligations for NAICS 541690 (Other Scientific and Technical Consulting Services) total $1.2B in FY2026 to date. Award activity shows 2,374 awards with an average award size of $505K. Obligations fell 44.6% year over year. Historical annual totals show FY21 at $1.9B, FY22 at $2B, FY23 at $2B, FY24 at $2.3B, and FY25 at $2.2B, so the current fiscal year-to-date total of $1.2B is lower than each of the prior full-year figures. This market is still concentrated among several large buyers and vendors. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer with $407M, followed by the Agency for International Development at $276M and the Department of Health and Human Services at $256M. On the supplier side, undisclosed domestic awardees lead with $275M, and named vendors include GENERAL DYNAMICS ONE SOURCE LLC at $87.7M and KELLY SERVICES, INC. at $61.3M. The FY2026 to date totals are partial because the fiscal year is ongoing.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has NAICS 541690 spending changed compared with prior years?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 44.6% year over year. The current fiscal year-to-date total is $1.2B, compared with $2.2B in FY25 and $2.3B in FY24. Earlier annual totals were $2B in FY23 and FY22 and $1.9B in FY21."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the biggest buyers and contractors in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The largest buying agencies are the Department of Defense with $407M, Agency for International Development with $276M, and Department of Health and Human Services with $256M. The top vendors are DOMESTIC AWARDEES (UNDISCLOSED) at $275M, GENERAL DYNAMICS ONE SOURCE LLC at $87.7M, and KELLY SERVICES, INC. at $61.3M."
      }
    ]
